course: dictionary
lesson: 9316
title: Spellbound and strong attention
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Spellbound means so interested or amazed by something that you cannot look away or think of anything else. Read the words around it to find the clues. «It seems alive — chattering, chuckling, sparkling — and he sits on the bank, spellbound, as if it were telling him stories.» The clues are sparkling and chuckling, and the sitting still. He is listening so hard that he cannot look away, so spellbound means completely captivated.
explain: Spellbound is a feelings word for strong attention. An audience can be spellbound by a great story or show, and you can hold someone spellbound when you keep them so interested that they forget everything else. Swap in a word like amazed or captivated and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Spellbound has a second meaning from fairy tales, where a person is held under a magic spell. Read the sentence first, then decide which meaning fits. Whenever you meet a word with two meanings, the context tells you which one the writer means.
fact: Spellbound means so interested or amazed that you cannot look away or think of anything else.
fact: In fairy tales, spellbound means held under a magic spell.
fact: «Hold someone spellbound» means to keep them completely interested.
fact: In The Wind in the Willows, Rat and Mole are spellbound by the music they hear on the river.
fact: A word can have more than one meaning, so check which one fits the sentence around it.
exercise: «It seems alive — chattering, chuckling, sparkling — and he sits on the bank, spellbound.» What does spellbound mean here? | Running fast along the bank | Bored and yawning | *So interested that you cannot look away | Cold and wet from the river
exercise: An audience is spellbound by a great story. What does spellbound show? | *Completely captivated and unable to look away | Asleep in their seats | Angry and shouting at the stage | Walking out of the room
exercise: In a fairy tale, someone is spellbound. What does this mean? | Very cold and hungry | Lost in a forest with no map | Covered in paint | *Held under a magic spell
test: Rat and Mole are spellbound by the music on the river. Which word could replace spellbound? | *Captivated | Sleepy | Hungry | Bored
test: Which best explains «hold someone spellbound»? | *Keep them so interested that they cannot look away | Make them laugh out loud | Make them bored and sleepy | Tie them up with rope
exam: «Hold someone spellbound» means to keep them so interested that they cannot look away, while in a fairy tale spellbound means held under a magic spell. Which meaning fits: «The audience sat spellbound through the whole show»? | Sleepy after a long lunch | Wet through from the rain | *So interested that they could not look away | Held under a magic spell in a tower
